# Architecture

Recallio is a Bun workspaces monorepo: `backend`, `frontend`, `shared`.

## Packages

- **`backend` (`@recallio/backend`)** — NestJS API: modules, config, Prisma, integrations.
- **`frontend` (`@recallio/frontend`)** — React + Vite dashboard.
- **`shared` (`@recallio/shared`)** — Zod schemas (`@recallio/shared/schemas`) and generated OpenAPI types (`@recallio/api-types` → `shared/src/types/api.d.ts`).

Do not invent new packages or cross-package layers. Keep app logic in `backend`/`frontend`; put only shared runtime schemas and API types in `shared`.

## Boundaries

- Controllers stay thin: validate input, call a use case, return DTOs.
- Business logic lives in **use cases** (`*.use-case.ts` or `use-cases/*.ts`).
- Persistence lives in **DAOs** (`*.dao.ts`). Do not call Prisma from controllers.
- External SDKs (Shopify, Anthropic, Clerk) stay behind module providers/clients/adapters — not in controllers or DAOs.
- Before proposing architectural changes, inspect the relevant existing module first.

## Shared package

- Add cross-cutting Zod schemas under `shared/src/schemas/` and re-export from `schemas/index.ts`.
- Regenerate OpenAPI types with root `api:generate` after backend route/DTO changes; do not hand-edit `api.d.ts`.
- Rebuild shared after schema changes: `bun run --cwd shared build`.

## Tooling

- Package manager: Bun. Root scripts use `bun --filter @recallio/...`.
- Backend ESM: Nest + TypeScript `nodenext`; relative imports use `.js` extensions.
- Do not introduce secrets into source. Env is validated in `backend/src/config/env.ts`.
